1
00:01:01,880 --> 00:01:05,880
Taming The Husband

2
00:01:06,880 --> 00:01:08,360
Episode 16

3
00:01:08,920 --> 00:01:10,000
Ma Jade Shop

4
00:01:10,120 --> 00:01:12,520
My uncle heard this morning
that the court's going to lift

5
00:01:12,600 --> 00:01:13,800
the ban on shipping
Lianghuai licensed salt,

6
00:01:14,360 --> 00:01:16,280
so from now on, licensed salt in Yangzhou

7
00:01:16,360 --> 00:01:18,080
-can be sold freely.
-What?

8
00:01:18,320 --> 00:01:20,520
Then salt will be as cheap as cabbage,
not worth a penny!

9
00:01:20,600 --> 00:01:22,040
Exactly.

10
00:01:22,120 --> 00:01:23,600
So many people have sunk
all their money into it,

11
00:01:23,760 --> 00:01:26,640
-hoping to make a little profit.
-My son's life savings went into this!

12
00:01:26,720 --> 00:01:28,960
If you don't pay us back,
I'll bash my head in right here!

13
00:01:29,040 --> 00:01:31,320
-Let us in!
-We want to go in!

14
00:01:31,600 --> 00:01:33,680
Sir! Sir, gentlemen!

15
00:01:33,920 --> 00:01:35,520
Please hear me out.

16
00:01:35,800 --> 00:01:36,880
Calm down, sir.

17
00:01:37,520 --> 00:01:39,160
If the price of salt went up,

18
00:01:39,240 --> 00:01:40,760
would you give me a share of the profits?

19
00:01:40,840 --> 00:01:42,320
My son put up his own money!

20
00:01:42,440 --> 00:01:45,080
Who do you think you are,
asking for a share?

21
00:01:45,160 --> 00:01:47,360
Fine. If the price goes up,

22
00:01:47,440 --> 00:01:48,640
I don't get a share,

23
00:01:48,720 --> 00:01:50,480
so if it goes down,
that's no concern of mine either.

24
00:01:50,560 --> 00:01:52,040
You can all go home.

25
00:01:52,120 --> 00:01:53,880
Wait! Wait!

26
00:01:53,960 --> 00:01:56,160
Yes, investors take their own risks,

27
00:01:56,720 --> 00:01:57,920
but a silly woman like you,

28
00:01:58,120 --> 00:01:59,360
so shortsighted,

29
00:01:59,920 --> 00:02:01,400
wouldn't know that in business,

30
00:02:01,480 --> 00:02:04,040
some things matter more than money,
like decency!

31
00:02:04,120 --> 00:02:06,280
-That's right!
-You have no decency!

32
00:02:06,360 --> 00:02:09,440
-No decency! None at all!
-No decency! None at all!

33
00:02:09,520 --> 00:02:12,080
-These losses are a crushing burden
-No decency! None at all!

34
00:02:12,680 --> 00:02:14,560
for ordinary people like us,

35
00:02:15,160 --> 00:02:16,360
but to the Xies,

36
00:02:16,440 --> 00:02:18,000
they're just a speck of dust,

37
00:02:18,560 --> 00:02:21,600
yet you won't part with even that!

38
00:02:21,760 --> 00:02:22,760
In that case,

39
00:02:22,840 --> 00:02:24,160
with so many other salt shops around,

40
00:02:24,240 --> 00:02:26,600
why should we put up with this treatment?

41
00:02:26,680 --> 00:02:28,480
-Exactly! No decency!
-Exactly! No decency!

42
00:02:28,560 --> 00:02:30,640
-No decency!
-No decency!

43
00:02:30,720 --> 00:02:32,240
-The others are all small shops,
-No decency!

44
00:02:32,520 --> 00:02:33,640
-so buying back permits won't cost much,
-No decency!

45
00:02:33,720 --> 00:02:34,920
-and it's worth it to keep the peace.
-No decency!

46
00:02:35,440 --> 00:02:41,280
-No decency!
-No decency!

47
00:02:41,360 --> 00:02:42,400
You… You…

48
00:02:42,640 --> 00:02:44,000
So you admit it?

49
00:02:44,080 --> 00:02:45,200
I do.

50
00:02:45,400 --> 00:02:46,640
I've got no decency,

51
00:02:46,720 --> 00:02:47,960
and I'm greedy, too!

52
00:02:48,040 --> 00:02:52,400
That's why even a single coin taken
out of my pocket breaks my heart,

53
00:02:52,960 --> 00:02:54,240
so no one understands better than I do

54
00:02:54,320 --> 00:02:55,560
what you're going through.

55
00:02:55,640 --> 00:02:57,840
So, please,

56
00:02:57,920 --> 00:02:59,080
give me half a month.

57
00:02:59,640 --> 00:03:01,000
-Half a month? That's too long!
-Yes.

58
00:03:01,360 --> 00:03:02,560
You crooked merchants

59
00:03:02,640 --> 00:03:03,840
make such pretty promises,

60
00:03:03,920 --> 00:03:04,920
but why should we believe you?

61
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:07,320
-Exactly! Why should we?
-That's right!

62
00:03:07,520 --> 00:03:09,240
I want to keep making money,
so I would never

63
00:03:09,320 --> 00:03:10,360
ruin the Xie name.

64
00:03:10,440 --> 00:03:11,440
So tell me,

65
00:03:11,520 --> 00:03:13,760
who would you be more likely to trust,

66
00:03:13,840 --> 00:03:15,160
someone who claims to act out of decency,

67
00:03:15,240 --> 00:03:16,720
or someone protecting her own interests?

68
00:03:17,200 --> 00:03:19,160
Think about it.

69
00:03:26,760 --> 00:03:27,880
What if she doesn't give it?

70
00:03:27,960 --> 00:03:29,640
I've managed to smooth things over

71
00:03:29,720 --> 00:03:31,000
with the officials, more or less.

72
00:03:31,560 --> 00:03:33,000
As for the salt permits we've collected,

73
00:03:33,080 --> 00:03:34,920
I'll have them sent
to your house in a few days.

74
00:03:35,640 --> 00:03:37,000
There's something else.

75
00:03:37,080 --> 00:03:39,240
We couldn't trace the rumor.

76
00:03:40,800 --> 00:03:43,640
You have the connections
to win over the officials,

77
00:03:44,200 --> 00:03:45,440
but you can't trace a rumor?

78
00:03:46,200 --> 00:03:47,440
How strange.

79
00:03:47,800 --> 00:03:48,840
One man points to another,

80
00:03:48,920 --> 00:03:51,040
and that man points to someone else,
who then claims

81
00:03:51,240 --> 00:03:52,680
he can't remember who told him.

82
00:03:53,720 --> 00:03:55,160
So this news that the court plans to lift

83
00:03:55,240 --> 00:03:56,720
the Lianghuai salt shipping ban

84
00:03:56,800 --> 00:03:58,120
might not be true?

85
00:03:58,240 --> 00:03:59,280
It might not be,

86
00:03:59,760 --> 00:04:01,360
but we can't say it's false either.

87
00:04:01,920 --> 00:04:04,000
Repeat a lie enough,
and people believe it,

88
00:04:04,240 --> 00:04:06,160
so if the rumor spreads

89
00:04:06,240 --> 00:04:07,360
and the price of salt really falls,

90
00:04:07,440 --> 00:04:08,520
the damage is real either way.

91
00:04:08,600 --> 00:04:09,960
Then I'll beat the petition drum

92
00:04:10,040 --> 00:04:11,680
and demand an official explanation!

93
00:04:12,400 --> 00:04:13,640
You'd drag the authorities into this

94
00:04:13,720 --> 00:04:15,160
over an unproven rumor?

95
00:04:15,720 --> 00:04:16,840
Go ahead, then,

96
00:04:16,920 --> 00:04:18,160
and I'll accuse you right back

97
00:04:18,240 --> 00:04:20,400
of colluding with officials

98
00:04:20,480 --> 00:04:22,000
to pry into state policy.

99
00:04:22,080 --> 00:04:23,480
Won't that be fun?

100
00:04:27,040 --> 00:04:28,240
We've been at this for ages.

101
00:04:28,320 --> 00:04:29,320
Come on.

102
00:04:29,440 --> 00:04:30,440
Our payment?

103
00:04:31,520 --> 00:04:32,880
You haven't even done the job properly,

104
00:04:32,960 --> 00:04:34,320
and you're asking for money?

105
00:04:35,520 --> 00:04:36,520
Boss Jin,

106
00:04:36,840 --> 00:04:38,640
yes, the lads and I

107
00:04:38,760 --> 00:04:40,240
do love money,

108
00:04:40,920 --> 00:04:42,960
but if word of a price collapse
really gets out,

109
00:04:43,080 --> 00:04:44,960
apart from watching you

110
00:04:45,640 --> 00:04:47,480
sweat and fly into a rage,

111
00:04:47,560 --> 00:04:48,720
what do we stand to gain?

112
00:04:49,280 --> 00:04:50,360
The more people demanding payment,

113
00:04:50,440 --> 00:04:52,240
the less likely we are to get ours!

114
00:04:52,960 --> 00:04:54,040
After all that work,

115
00:04:54,240 --> 00:04:55,720
do you think we had nothing better to do?

116
00:05:00,160 --> 00:05:01,200
Fine, then.

117
00:05:04,320 --> 00:05:07,600
Maybe your own roof is leaking,

118
00:05:07,680 --> 00:05:09,360
and you're blaming the rain.

119
00:05:10,160 --> 00:05:11,280
Let's go.

120
00:05:11,880 --> 00:05:13,880
Xie Salt Shop

121
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:31,520
Why aren't you back yet?

122
00:05:41,680 --> 00:05:42,680
My lady.

123
00:05:53,440 --> 00:05:54,600
With Yan away

124
00:05:55,520 --> 00:05:57,120
and something this serious happening,

125
00:05:58,120 --> 00:05:59,800
why didn't you come and talk to me?

126
00:06:02,360 --> 00:06:04,040
I know young women

127
00:06:04,440 --> 00:06:05,600
can be easily embarrassed.

128
00:06:06,400 --> 00:06:07,560
That's not it, my lady.

129
00:06:08,720 --> 00:06:11,040
I thought this through before I acted.

130
00:06:11,600 --> 00:06:13,400
I know I made some big promises.

131
00:06:13,480 --> 00:06:15,200
Now that things have gone wrong,

132
00:06:15,520 --> 00:06:17,400
embarrassment wouldn't matter,
since I'm not afraid of it.

133
00:06:18,240 --> 00:06:20,080
It's just that if I can't put this right,

134
00:06:20,640 --> 00:06:22,120
after all our efforts,
the shop we finally got

135
00:06:22,200 --> 00:06:23,400
will be taken away,

136
00:06:23,480 --> 00:06:25,040
and Xie Yan will suffer, too.

137
00:06:25,640 --> 00:06:28,360
So I wanted to sort it out first,
then tell you.

138
00:06:29,840 --> 00:06:31,760
What matters now--

139
00:06:31,840 --> 00:06:34,000
Your uncle and Aunt Shen
set a trap for you,

140
00:06:34,080 --> 00:06:36,080
and you fell right into it.

141
00:06:37,640 --> 00:06:40,000
Even brothers keep separate accounts,

142
00:06:40,480 --> 00:06:41,480
especially

143
00:06:41,800 --> 00:06:43,080
when there's a fortune at stake.

144
00:06:44,560 --> 00:06:45,560
Baozhu,

145
00:06:46,040 --> 00:06:49,160
I may be too sickly
to manage things often,

146
00:06:49,840 --> 00:06:51,000
but I'm not oblivious.

147
00:07:00,120 --> 00:07:01,440
Sit down.

148
00:07:05,600 --> 00:07:07,960
I'm not saying this to blame you,

149
00:07:08,640 --> 00:07:10,040
but to let you know

150
00:07:10,320 --> 00:07:11,800
that even with Yan away,

151
00:07:11,880 --> 00:07:15,120
you still have me to rely on.

152
00:07:16,240 --> 00:07:17,640
If you can't trust me,

153
00:07:18,200 --> 00:07:20,040
there's Yi, and Yan's father,

154
00:07:20,120 --> 00:07:21,320
because we're family,

155
00:07:22,240 --> 00:07:23,240
and family

156
00:07:23,520 --> 00:07:24,920
would never let one of their own

157
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:26,040
be taken advantage of.

158
00:07:27,760 --> 00:07:28,880
Don't worry.

159
00:07:28,960 --> 00:07:31,840
We won't let this slide.

160
00:07:34,560 --> 00:07:37,240
But if this gets any worse,

161
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:39,640
it won't just hurt Yan,

162
00:07:39,720 --> 00:07:42,040
but the entire Xie family,

163
00:07:42,360 --> 00:07:44,680
and then we'd really be in trouble.

164
00:07:46,040 --> 00:07:49,000
Before this reaches Grandmother,

165
00:07:49,560 --> 00:07:51,000
let's act quickly,

166
00:07:51,240 --> 00:07:53,720
raise the money to pay them off,

167
00:07:53,800 --> 00:07:55,960
then focus on the problem.

168
00:07:56,440 --> 00:07:57,920
Once we have proof,

169
00:07:58,000 --> 00:08:00,360
we can tell Grandmother everything.

170
00:08:02,520 --> 00:08:03,800
It's just…

171
00:08:05,560 --> 00:08:06,560
What is it?

172
00:08:07,080 --> 00:08:09,600
Is there some difficulty,
or something you need me to do?

173
00:08:10,160 --> 00:08:11,360
With something this serious,

174
00:08:12,320 --> 00:08:16,160
I'm afraid
you can't run the salt shop anymore.

175
00:08:17,520 --> 00:08:18,920
It's not that I don't trust you.

176
00:08:19,120 --> 00:08:20,120
I understand.

177
00:08:21,600 --> 00:08:22,880
I haven't managed it properly,

178
00:08:25,720 --> 00:08:27,040
so I'll have to ask you

179
00:08:29,440 --> 00:08:30,440
to take over, my lady.

180
00:08:31,840 --> 00:08:33,440
But without the shop,

181
00:08:34,440 --> 00:08:36,240
how will I raise the money?

182
00:08:40,280 --> 00:08:41,560
My dear,

183
00:08:42,440 --> 00:08:44,560
Yan is my son, too,

184
00:08:44,840 --> 00:08:45,840
so his father and I

185
00:08:46,040 --> 00:08:48,040
should cover half for him,

186
00:08:48,520 --> 00:08:51,000
and you'll make up the rest.

187
00:08:54,720 --> 00:08:55,840
Don't worry.

188
00:08:57,040 --> 00:08:59,000
I'll find you another shop,

189
00:08:59,560 --> 00:09:02,320
though I'm afraid you'll have to make do.

190
00:09:02,880 --> 00:09:04,800
After what's happened,

191
00:09:05,200 --> 00:09:08,000
the shop you're given

192
00:09:08,440 --> 00:09:10,120
may not be as good as this one.

193
00:09:17,560 --> 00:09:19,520
You've opened too soon.

194
00:09:21,200 --> 00:09:22,720
This isn't the right time.

195
00:09:26,040 --> 00:09:28,120
This isn't the right time.

196
00:09:42,640 --> 00:09:43,640
I

197
00:09:46,800 --> 00:09:48,080
really

198
00:09:51,640 --> 00:09:52,840
miss

199
00:09:55,360 --> 00:09:56,480
you.

200
00:10:02,400 --> 00:10:03,800
Zhou General Store Flower Garden

201
00:10:14,320 --> 00:10:16,160
Can this shop get any customers?

202
00:10:17,720 --> 00:10:18,920
The location's probably too remote

203
00:10:19,240 --> 00:10:20,600
for even the finest wine to draw a crowd.

204
00:10:21,960 --> 00:10:23,680
What's so good about this wine?

205
00:10:23,760 --> 00:10:25,360
It certainly is out of the way.

206
00:10:26,640 --> 00:10:29,120
It's all old stock that won't sell,

207
00:10:29,680 --> 00:10:31,040
so how can we buy anything new?

208
00:10:31,600 --> 00:10:33,840
We might as well sell scrap!

209
00:10:36,040 --> 00:10:37,640
What do we do now?

210
00:10:39,400 --> 00:10:40,400
Here.

211
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:45,600
The other old stock may be worthless,

212
00:10:45,680 --> 00:10:46,800
but fermented black beans

213
00:10:47,200 --> 00:10:48,920
get better with age.

214
00:10:49,000 --> 00:10:50,280
Smell them.

215
00:10:52,400 --> 00:10:54,360
What is that moldy smell?

216
00:10:54,440 --> 00:10:56,320
It's fermented tofu.
Haven't you heard of it?

217
00:10:57,240 --> 00:10:58,480
It's like stinky tofu,

218
00:10:58,560 --> 00:11:00,360
which smells awful but tastes great.

219
00:11:08,720 --> 00:11:10,000
It must be worth a fortune!

220
00:11:10,080 --> 00:11:11,120
Is it good?

221
00:11:18,960 --> 00:11:20,240
It's… delicious.

222
00:11:20,360 --> 00:11:22,600
-Delicious.
-Let me try.

223
00:11:38,760 --> 00:11:40,000
Young master,

224
00:11:43,760 --> 00:11:44,960
are you feeling less seasick?

225
00:11:45,520 --> 00:11:46,520
I still feel a little sick,

226
00:11:47,040 --> 00:11:48,160
but I'll have to get used to it.

227
00:11:48,240 --> 00:11:51,200
Just hold on a little longer.
One more day, and we'll be in Yangzhou.

228
00:12:04,160 --> 00:12:05,440
It can't come soon enough.

229
00:12:06,920 --> 00:12:09,440
We're bringing back a full cargo,
so it's been a worthwhile trip.

230
00:12:16,080 --> 00:12:17,720
It's only a decent start,

231
00:12:18,280 --> 00:12:19,520
but with this trip to our credit,

232
00:12:20,520 --> 00:12:22,160
it'll be easier to secure the next job.

233
00:12:24,040 --> 00:12:25,640
Young master! Young master!

234
00:12:25,720 --> 00:12:27,880
It's pouring,
and there's a huge hole in the hold roof!

235
00:12:29,280 --> 00:12:31,320
-Cover everything, quickly!
-Give it here!

236
00:12:32,800 --> 00:12:34,800
-Hurry! Cover it all with tarpaulins!
-Yes! Yes!

237
00:12:36,440 --> 00:12:38,160
-Get the oilcloth! Hurry!
-Yes! Yes!

238
00:12:47,240 --> 00:12:48,640
Come on! Move faster!

239
00:12:50,280 --> 00:12:54,040
Everyone, listen to me! Captain,
go and seal that hole in the roof!

240
00:12:54,120 --> 00:12:56,120
East and west hold crews, take your sides!
Bail out the water and plug the leaks!

241
00:12:56,200 --> 00:12:58,840
Everyone else, bring anything
that needs to stay dry up onto the deck!

242
00:12:58,920 --> 00:13:00,680
Jianwei, come below with me

243
00:13:00,760 --> 00:13:02,360
-to check for leaks.
-Yes.

244
00:13:02,440 --> 00:13:04,440
Young master! Go back inside,
or you'll catch a chill in this rain.

245
00:13:04,520 --> 00:13:05,640
Only paper tigers are afraid of water.

246
00:13:05,960 --> 00:13:06,960
Worry about yourself!

247
00:13:07,240 --> 00:13:08,360
Hurry! Come on! Move!

248
00:13:08,440 --> 00:13:09,760
Cover the goods over there!

249
00:13:10,240 --> 00:13:12,520
-Quickly! Get moving!
-Hurry!

250
00:13:13,640 --> 00:13:14,640
You men,

251
00:13:14,840 --> 00:13:16,040
come help me patch the roof!

252
00:13:16,120 --> 00:13:17,600
-Hurry!
-Yes!

253
00:13:21,120 --> 00:13:22,320
Yan

254
00:13:27,320 --> 00:13:29,040
Thanks to your luck, young master,

255
00:13:29,200 --> 00:13:30,640
the rain stopped just in time,

256
00:13:30,720 --> 00:13:32,480
and your quick thinking

257
00:13:32,560 --> 00:13:34,000
averted a disaster.

258
00:13:34,240 --> 00:13:36,040
Only these spices got soaked,

259
00:13:36,440 --> 00:13:37,680
but that oilcloth

260
00:13:37,760 --> 00:13:39,280
won't hold much longer,

261
00:13:39,360 --> 00:13:42,120
so to be safe,
we should put ashore for repairs soon.

262
00:13:42,680 --> 00:13:44,040
I'm afraid

263
00:13:44,160 --> 00:13:45,600
that'll set us back a few days.

264
00:13:46,280 --> 00:13:47,280
Yes.

265
00:13:49,000 --> 00:13:50,080
Just as you wanted?

266
00:13:51,440 --> 00:13:52,760
What?

267
00:13:52,840 --> 00:13:54,040
You've been at this for years,

268
00:13:54,640 --> 00:13:56,400
so why would a little rain
throw you into a panic?

269
00:13:57,240 --> 00:13:59,120
It was nothing more
than an ordinary downpour,

270
00:13:59,200 --> 00:14:02,880
so how could it
tear a hole in a wooden roof?

271
00:14:02,960 --> 00:14:04,800
And if the hole was already there,

272
00:14:04,880 --> 00:14:06,240
with you making your rounds day and night,

273
00:14:06,920 --> 00:14:08,560
why didn't you ever tell me?

274
00:14:10,720 --> 00:14:12,040
How much did they promise you?

275
00:14:12,640 --> 00:14:13,640
A hundred taels.

276
00:14:14,200 --> 00:14:17,480
Young master,
punish me however you see fit.

277
00:14:17,560 --> 00:14:19,440
Do you know why I'm laughing?

278
00:14:20,040 --> 00:14:21,520
You think I'm beneath you.

279
00:14:21,600 --> 00:14:22,640
No.

280
00:14:23,760 --> 00:14:25,160
You have ambition,

281
00:14:25,920 --> 00:14:27,000
and the nerve to act on it.

282
00:14:28,240 --> 00:14:32,000
It would be a pity
if you were loyal to my uncle,

283
00:14:32,440 --> 00:14:33,960
but luckily, you aren't.

284
00:14:35,080 --> 00:14:37,120
There'll be plenty of money to come,

285
00:14:37,840 --> 00:14:39,000
and I can give you

286
00:14:39,120 --> 00:14:40,760
more than he ever could.

287
00:14:42,240 --> 00:14:45,720
After all, you know what my uncle is like.

288
00:14:46,280 --> 00:14:48,000
You'd still employ me, young master?

289
00:14:48,560 --> 00:14:49,720
Of course.

290
00:14:50,560 --> 00:14:52,160
Why do you think I made you fix the roof?

291
00:14:53,960 --> 00:14:54,960
If you'd failed,

292
00:14:55,440 --> 00:14:57,000
you'd never work on a boat again.

293
00:14:57,720 --> 00:14:58,920
But you fixed it,

294
00:14:59,160 --> 00:15:00,840
so there's still a way back for you.

295
00:15:08,240 --> 00:15:09,640
Someone once told me,

296
00:15:10,760 --> 00:15:11,960
"Sometimes it's wise to play the fool,"

297
00:15:13,720 --> 00:15:15,280
so I'm giving you another chance.

298
00:15:16,320 --> 00:15:17,760
But every coin spent on repairs

299
00:15:18,960 --> 00:15:21,440
will come out of your allowance.

300
00:15:26,160 --> 00:15:27,160
Young master,

301
00:15:28,000 --> 00:15:30,120
it was Lady Lin,
acting on First Master Xie's orders,

302
00:15:30,200 --> 00:15:31,800
who told me to delay your return.

303
00:15:31,960 --> 00:15:33,240
Why?

304
00:15:33,760 --> 00:15:35,760
I don't know.

305
00:15:39,320 --> 00:15:40,640
<i>Baozhu.</i>

306
00:15:45,960 --> 00:15:48,440
When is anyone going to come in?

307
00:15:48,520 --> 00:15:50,080
Forget making money.

308
00:15:50,640 --> 00:15:52,200
I'll be lucky

309
00:15:52,280 --> 00:15:53,560
if I don't lose what I put in.

310
00:15:53,640 --> 00:15:54,760
Until we turn a profit,

311
00:15:55,240 --> 00:15:56,640
I can work without pay.

312
00:15:57,640 --> 00:15:58,840
How very kind.

313
00:15:58,920 --> 00:15:59,920
Forget a profit,

314
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:01,560
I'm afraid I'll lose

315
00:16:05,320 --> 00:16:06,560
this shop, too.

316
00:16:06,640 --> 00:16:08,560
Just what I was afraid of.

317
00:16:09,200 --> 00:16:10,600
You little…

318
00:16:25,680 --> 00:16:27,480
Look, this is the one.

319
00:16:34,000 --> 00:16:36,080
This perfumed powder is made from flowers.

320
00:16:38,240 --> 00:16:40,240
-Here.
-Wouldn't it be wasted

321
00:16:41,240 --> 00:16:42,560
on a face like that?

322
00:16:44,680 --> 00:16:45,680
It's wasted on someone who looks fine

323
00:16:45,760 --> 00:16:47,880
but is rotten to the core.

324
00:16:47,960 --> 00:16:49,880
We're beautiful inside and out,
so why shouldn't we use it?

325
00:16:49,960 --> 00:16:51,440
We certainly will!

326
00:16:51,520 --> 00:16:52,960
If you like it, buy it.

327
00:16:54,560 --> 00:16:56,760
What a coincidence that our shops

328
00:16:56,840 --> 00:16:58,080
are so close together.

329
00:16:58,160 --> 00:17:00,680
Whenever you're free, do drop by.

330
00:17:01,320 --> 00:17:02,760
Xie General Store

331
00:17:07,080 --> 00:17:08,920
No escaping an enemy, is there?

332
00:17:12,040 --> 00:17:14,720
Have we ever been enemies?

333
00:17:14,800 --> 00:17:16,080
Since we're in the same trade,

334
00:17:16,160 --> 00:17:17,320
that makes us rivals.

335
00:17:17,440 --> 00:17:18,480
Good day.

336
00:17:20,080 --> 00:17:21,720
Leaving already? Nothing else you like?

337
00:17:21,840 --> 00:17:24,080
We're already so far out of the way,
so what are we going to do after this?

338
00:17:24,160 --> 00:17:25,160
Don't worry.

339
00:17:39,600 --> 00:17:40,600
Come and see our flowers!

340
00:17:40,680 --> 00:17:42,120
Sweet-smelling and freshly picked!

341
00:17:42,200 --> 00:17:43,400
Take a few stems home!

342
00:17:43,640 --> 00:17:45,360
Do you see anything, miss, that you like?

343
00:17:45,440 --> 00:17:47,640
These are still too big,
so let's take these instead.

344
00:17:47,720 --> 00:17:49,200
Take your time choosing

345
00:17:49,280 --> 00:17:50,400
and look around all you like.

346
00:17:50,480 --> 00:17:51,480
All right.

347
00:17:52,840 --> 00:17:54,880
-This one's nice.
-Let's buy it, then.

348
00:18:06,120 --> 00:18:08,520
Smell these for me
and tell me which of the two is sweeter.

349
00:18:11,440 --> 00:18:13,480
Flowers! Fresh flowers!

350
00:18:13,880 --> 00:18:15,360
Freshly picked!

351
00:18:34,400 --> 00:18:36,000
All right, that'll do.

352
00:18:36,280 --> 00:18:38,000
Let's see if we can
make some perfumed powder.

353
00:18:38,320 --> 00:18:40,440
Otherwise, Yingtao will wonder
where we are.

354
00:18:42,480 --> 00:18:43,480
Here you are, sir.

355
00:18:44,080 --> 00:18:45,320
Come again!

356
00:18:46,280 --> 00:18:47,840
-Slow down!
-My legs are numb!

357
00:18:49,600 --> 00:18:52,360
-Let me carry this.
-Flowers! Fresh flowers!

358
00:18:53,400 --> 00:18:54,640
Come and take a look!

359
00:18:55,200 --> 00:18:56,480
My lady! My lady!

360
00:18:57,640 --> 00:19:00,000
My lady! He's back!

361
00:19:00,560 --> 00:19:02,400
-Who's back?
-The young master's back!

362
00:19:02,480 --> 00:19:04,440
-Where?
-There!

363
00:19:05,840 --> 00:19:06,840
Xie Yan!

364
00:19:10,720 --> 00:19:12,120
Xie Yan!

365
00:19:13,320 --> 00:19:15,120
Xie Yan!

366
00:19:23,520 --> 00:19:25,720
"In springtime joy, my horse flies by.

367
00:19:26,280 --> 00:19:28,520
In one day, all Chang'an's flowers
are mine to see."

368
00:19:29,280 --> 00:19:30,720
That scoundrel.

369
00:19:31,080 --> 00:19:33,360
Well? Have I gotten a bit of a tan?

370
00:19:35,720 --> 00:19:37,880
-Don't like me anymore?
-Of course I do.

371
00:19:38,280 --> 00:19:39,600
Black at both ends.

372
00:19:40,920 --> 00:19:42,440
Black at both ends?

373
00:19:42,800 --> 00:19:44,480
"Black at the ends, white in the middle,

374
00:19:44,560 --> 00:19:46,520
and the tastiest kind, a Jinhua pig!"

375
00:19:48,000 --> 00:19:49,480
Jin Baozhu!

376
00:19:51,040 --> 00:19:53,400
Such a big horse! How majestic!

377
00:19:59,600 --> 00:20:01,680
-Want a ride?
-Yes!

378
00:20:01,760 --> 00:20:03,160
Come on.

379
00:20:06,760 --> 00:20:07,760
Sit up.

380
00:20:14,440 --> 00:20:15,440
Hold tight.

381
00:20:22,040 --> 00:20:23,160
Well?

382
00:20:23,720 --> 00:20:24,720
Having fun?

383
00:20:31,440 --> 00:20:32,760
Faster! Faster!

384
00:20:33,400 --> 00:20:35,120
Jinxiu Clothing Shop Rice

385
00:20:35,200 --> 00:20:36,960
Still not fast enough!

386
00:20:40,720 --> 00:20:42,040
Xie Yan!

387
00:20:45,280 --> 00:20:46,920
So fast!

388
00:20:54,080 --> 00:20:56,040
The Xie Estate

389
00:21:00,280 --> 00:21:02,760
So, I've learned my lesson this time,

390
00:21:02,840 --> 00:21:05,160
and I'll do this properly,
because failure isn't an option.

391
00:21:22,760 --> 00:21:27,680
Why not leave it until tomorrow?

392
00:21:28,400 --> 00:21:29,400
Let's go back to our room and rest.

393
00:21:30,880 --> 00:21:32,760
I doubt I'd get much rest there.

394
00:21:33,720 --> 00:21:34,720
Why wouldn't you?

395
00:21:36,480 --> 00:21:39,440
Look, I can barely keep my eyes open,

396
00:21:40,920 --> 00:21:41,960
let alone sit up.

397
00:21:42,840 --> 00:21:44,000
Let's go and rest.

398
00:21:44,080 --> 00:21:45,520
Let's go and rest.

399
00:21:45,600 --> 00:21:47,240
-Sit up properly.
-No.

400
00:21:47,320 --> 00:21:48,760
-Sit up.
-No.

401
00:21:49,400 --> 00:21:50,680
Come on.

402
00:21:54,160 --> 00:21:55,320
Listen to me.

403
00:21:55,840 --> 00:21:56,880
I'm busy right now

404
00:21:56,960 --> 00:21:58,120
and haven't got time for you.

405
00:21:58,200 --> 00:22:00,600
If you're tired, go to bed by yourself.

406
00:22:01,920 --> 00:22:03,560
I'm not tired now, so I'll help.

407
00:22:04,440 --> 00:22:06,200
No, thanks,
you always make more work for me.

408
00:22:09,800 --> 00:22:10,880
You,

409
00:22:13,800 --> 00:22:15,960
less sweet talk, more work.

410
00:22:16,040 --> 00:22:18,640
-Behave yourself.
-As you command.

411
00:22:24,960 --> 00:22:27,040
Would you say I'm just a pretty face now?

412
00:22:29,600 --> 00:22:31,600
How about now?
Now that we've got the fragrance,

413
00:22:31,680 --> 00:22:35,000
the real question is
how to get people to smell it.

414
00:22:38,360 --> 00:22:39,680
First, distill it into floral water

415
00:22:40,320 --> 00:22:41,320
to add to tea or wine,

416
00:22:41,560 --> 00:22:42,600
then crush the petals

417
00:22:42,680 --> 00:22:44,880
for scented pendants and sachets,

418
00:22:45,240 --> 00:22:47,040
before drying the rest into a powder

419
00:22:47,240 --> 00:22:48,320
to scent the bedding.

420
00:22:49,440 --> 00:22:50,520
It's not a bad idea,

421
00:22:50,960 --> 00:22:52,640
just too good an idea.

422
00:22:53,240 --> 00:22:55,080
Too good in what way? Tell me more.

423
00:22:55,960 --> 00:22:57,720
It's too refined,

424
00:22:57,800 --> 00:22:59,600
and while wealthy customers would love it,

425
00:22:59,680 --> 00:23:00,800
I can't pull it off.

426
00:23:00,880 --> 00:23:03,240
Besides, those customers already

427
00:23:03,320 --> 00:23:04,400
buy from Aunt Shen.

428
00:23:06,400 --> 00:23:07,520
Young master!

429
00:23:07,920 --> 00:23:09,840
Young master! There's trouble at the dock.

430
00:23:12,080 --> 00:23:13,760
Yizhi fruit, lesser galangal,

431
00:23:14,160 --> 00:23:15,400
sand ginger, <i>tsaoko</i> cardamom.

432
00:23:15,480 --> 00:23:17,920
These spices come from
remote Yunnan and Guangdong,

433
00:23:18,040 --> 00:23:19,160
so they're rarely seen in Yangzhou.

434
00:23:22,840 --> 00:23:24,440
Didn't you go to Huaizhou?

435
00:23:24,520 --> 00:23:25,880
How did you end up with these?

436
00:23:26,440 --> 00:23:28,000
There was a merchant there
from Yunnan and Guangdong,

437
00:23:28,120 --> 00:23:29,560
whose spices weren't selling in Huaizhou,

438
00:23:30,120 --> 00:23:31,200
so I brought some here to try.

439
00:23:32,080 --> 00:23:33,840
I thought only one batch of goods
got soaked.

440
00:23:34,400 --> 00:23:35,480
Why is there so much?

441
00:23:35,960 --> 00:23:38,200
When the crew
saw the young master buying spices,

442
00:23:38,280 --> 00:23:39,640
they spent their own money on some, too,

443
00:23:40,200 --> 00:23:42,200
hoping to bring them back to Yangzhou
and make a profit.

444
00:23:42,920 --> 00:23:46,000
When the downpour hit,
everyone was busy saving our cargo,

445
00:23:46,080 --> 00:23:47,760
while their own spices got soaked.

446
00:23:47,920 --> 00:23:49,520
Together with the first batch,

447
00:23:50,080 --> 00:23:51,480
that's how we ended up with all this.

448
00:23:52,040 --> 00:23:54,200
Young master,
I'll send the crew home for now.

449
00:23:54,280 --> 00:23:56,160
No! We can't just leave them to it.

450
00:23:56,440 --> 00:23:57,480
It may be a headache,

451
00:23:57,560 --> 00:23:59,320
but at worst, we'll find a way together.

452
00:24:02,040 --> 00:24:04,680
You think I'd just shrug it off

453
00:24:05,240 --> 00:24:06,280
because it's not my problem?

454
00:24:06,840 --> 00:24:08,160
Is that what you think of me?

455
00:24:10,440 --> 00:24:11,440
You silly goose.

456
00:24:12,920 --> 00:24:15,280
Jianwei, tell them not to worry,

457
00:24:15,840 --> 00:24:17,080
because once our client pays us,

458
00:24:17,400 --> 00:24:18,640
I'll give them their share of the profits.

459
00:24:20,120 --> 00:24:21,120
Yes.

460
00:24:30,080 --> 00:24:31,400
Why are you looking at me?

461
00:24:32,520 --> 00:24:34,760
So a few days apart

462
00:24:34,840 --> 00:24:36,120
really can change how you see someone.

463
00:24:37,880 --> 00:24:39,560
And it seems you're no longer

464
00:24:40,080 --> 00:24:41,320
the ignorant boy you used to be either.

465
00:24:45,400 --> 00:24:47,000
Salt money to refund,

466
00:24:47,520 --> 00:24:48,920
loans to collect,

467
00:24:49,720 --> 00:24:51,160
interest to pay…

468
00:24:52,000 --> 00:24:53,640
When it rains, it pours,

469
00:24:53,760 --> 00:24:54,960
right on this poor merchant!

470
00:25:00,480 --> 00:25:03,040
Xie Yan, got the stomach
to clean pig guts?

471
00:25:03,680 --> 00:25:05,040
What?

472
00:25:15,280 --> 00:25:16,840
Maybe these spices didn't sell in Huaizhou

473
00:25:16,920 --> 00:25:18,680
because no one knew how to use them.

474
00:25:19,280 --> 00:25:21,920
Lesser galangal is warm and pungent,
cutting the grease and boosting flavor.

475
00:25:22,480 --> 00:25:23,480
Sand ginger has a distinct aroma

476
00:25:23,560 --> 00:25:24,880
and a sweet aftertaste.

477
00:25:32,200 --> 00:25:34,960
-Jianwei, is it ready?
-Coming, my lady!

478
00:25:37,560 --> 00:25:38,760
It's washed perfectly clean.

479
00:25:39,240 --> 00:25:40,320
Good.

480
00:25:51,280 --> 00:25:52,280
Put the lid on.

481
00:26:05,280 --> 00:26:06,280
Enjoy, everyone.

482
00:26:15,920 --> 00:26:17,040
-Delicious!
-So good!

483
00:26:17,120 --> 00:26:19,560
No gamey taste, and such a lovely aroma.

484
00:26:20,120 --> 00:26:21,280
That's the <i>tsaoko </i>cardamom Baozhu added.

485
00:26:21,680 --> 00:26:24,360
-This spice--
-That's the <i>tsaoko </i>cardamom Baozhu added.

486
00:26:24,560 --> 00:26:26,400
Baozhu this, Baozhu that,

487
00:26:26,960 --> 00:26:28,040
you're making me sick!

488
00:26:28,200 --> 00:26:31,640
I think you put a lot of work
into this, too, Yan.

489
00:26:31,720 --> 00:26:33,080
Asking for a beating?

490
00:26:34,160 --> 00:26:35,160
Are you asking for one?

491
00:26:35,240 --> 00:26:37,680
-Jin Baozhu, help me hit him!
-Get him!

492
00:26:37,800 --> 00:26:39,720
-You--, I--
-Eat!

493
00:26:40,880 --> 00:26:41,880
Fine, I'll eat.

494
00:26:45,240 --> 00:26:46,240
It's really good.

495
00:26:46,480 --> 00:26:47,480
Delicious!

496
00:26:48,040 --> 00:26:49,920
-I'll have another bowl.
-Isn't it delicious?

497
00:26:50,000 --> 00:26:51,000
It is!

498
00:26:52,200 --> 00:26:53,360
Take that!

499
00:26:53,440 --> 00:26:55,360
-You asked for it!
-Take this.

500
00:26:57,200 --> 00:26:58,880
--Eat it all up!
-I'll have another bowl.

501
00:26:59,600 --> 00:27:01,920
-Especially you!
-Look, I've finished!

502
00:27:02,400 --> 00:27:03,400
Eat! Eat! Eat!

503
00:27:04,920 --> 00:27:06,320
Xie General Store

504
00:27:06,400 --> 00:27:08,600
I, Shen Manyun, don't sell ordinary goods,

505
00:27:09,000 --> 00:27:10,640
and everything in this shop

506
00:27:10,720 --> 00:27:13,640
is the very best,
sourced far and wide by my husband.

507
00:27:14,400 --> 00:27:16,040
This Jade Dew powder

508
00:27:16,320 --> 00:27:18,040
uses the finest white jasmine,

509
00:27:18,600 --> 00:27:20,680
pearl powder, and ambergris,

510
00:27:20,760 --> 00:27:22,040
finely ground

511
00:27:22,120 --> 00:27:23,760
and passed through three silk sieves

512
00:27:23,840 --> 00:27:25,800
to yield just five or six boxes.

513
00:27:25,880 --> 00:27:27,200
I even use it myself.

514
00:27:27,280 --> 00:27:29,120
Then order two more boxes for me.

515
00:27:31,080 --> 00:27:33,160
What's that wonderful smell?

516
00:27:35,240 --> 00:27:36,800
I'll wrap these up for you.

517
00:27:41,000 --> 00:27:43,120
Enjoy your food, everyone!

518
00:27:43,200 --> 00:27:45,160
Coming right up! Love it or it's free!

519
00:27:45,520 --> 00:27:47,640
-I'll add some spices.
-Come and try some!

520
00:27:47,800 --> 00:27:49,080
Love it or it's free!

521
00:27:49,160 --> 00:27:50,840
Don't miss your chance!

522
00:27:53,960 --> 00:27:55,640
Where did my lady get so much firewood?

523
00:27:55,720 --> 00:27:57,280
She chops wood when she's angry,

524
00:27:57,360 --> 00:27:59,160
just thirty or forty baskets' worth.

525
00:27:59,240 --> 00:28:01,800
Thirty or forty baskets? Impressive!

526
00:28:03,560 --> 00:28:04,560
Let me help.

527
00:28:05,840 --> 00:28:06,840
Look at you.

528
00:28:07,600 --> 00:28:08,720
-All right!
-It's fine.

529
00:28:09,040 --> 00:28:10,400
All right.

530
00:28:17,800 --> 00:28:18,800
Here.

531
00:28:18,880 --> 00:28:19,920
Pork offal stew

532
00:28:29,720 --> 00:28:31,760
<i>My lady, the young master sent this.</i>

533
00:28:31,840 --> 00:28:32,840
<i>Wipe off your sweat.</i>

534
00:28:36,120 --> 00:28:38,440
Here you are.

535
00:28:38,880 --> 00:28:39,880
Enjoy.

536
00:28:55,400 --> 00:28:57,240
All that excessive sweating, young master,

537
00:28:57,320 --> 00:28:59,400
could be a sign of kidney qi deficiency.

538
00:28:59,960 --> 00:29:02,040
You really should
take better care of yourself

539
00:29:02,120 --> 00:29:03,840
and avoid overexertion.

540
00:29:03,920 --> 00:29:05,080
I'm Baozhu's husband,

541
00:29:05,640 --> 00:29:07,200
so working hard for her is my duty.

542
00:29:08,320 --> 00:29:09,720
No need to worry, Master Song,

543
00:29:10,280 --> 00:29:11,480
just look after yourself.

544
00:29:12,600 --> 00:29:13,600
By the way,

545
00:29:14,120 --> 00:29:16,000
this handkerchief
was embroidered by my mother.

546
00:29:16,560 --> 00:29:18,320
If you like it, you can have it.

547
00:29:18,400 --> 00:29:19,640
Don't be shy.

548
00:29:41,240 --> 00:29:42,480
Aunt Shen, it's you!

549
00:29:42,800 --> 00:29:43,960
What a coincidence. Come!

550
00:29:44,240 --> 00:29:45,280
Let me get you something to try.

551
00:29:45,720 --> 00:29:47,000
How thoughtful, Yi.

552
00:29:47,120 --> 00:29:50,080
No, thank you.
These clothes are brand-new.

553
00:29:50,560 --> 00:29:52,320
Is a bowl of pork offal

554
00:29:52,400 --> 00:29:53,440
worth fighting through that crowd

555
00:29:53,720 --> 00:29:55,240
and ruining them?

556
00:29:55,560 --> 00:29:57,520
Pork offal may be nothing special,

557
00:29:57,600 --> 00:29:59,640
but we've got a secret recipe.

558
00:30:01,280 --> 00:30:02,440
How do you make a broth

559
00:30:02,520 --> 00:30:03,680
that smells so good from miles away?

560
00:30:03,760 --> 00:30:04,920
-I'd like some, too!
-It smells wonderful

561
00:30:05,160 --> 00:30:06,880
-Me, too!
-Take a look!

562
00:30:07,040 --> 00:30:08,560
Come and take a look!

563
00:30:08,640 --> 00:30:10,760
Ma'am, how do you make
this pork offal stew?

564
00:30:10,840 --> 00:30:13,320
-It smells wonderful!
-What a wonderful smell!

565
00:30:13,400 --> 00:30:14,440
My husband

566
00:30:14,520 --> 00:30:15,640
traveled widely in his youth,

567
00:30:16,200 --> 00:30:17,480
so he knows a thing or two

568
00:30:17,560 --> 00:30:18,560
about the customs of different places.

569
00:30:18,640 --> 00:30:20,480
From Shu's fragrant, numbing heat

570
00:30:20,560 --> 00:30:21,960
to the North's rich braised flavors,

571
00:30:22,040 --> 00:30:23,240
we've got them all!

572
00:30:23,320 --> 00:30:24,520
I'm her husband.

573
00:30:26,400 --> 00:30:27,680
Look at this man.

574
00:30:28,680 --> 00:30:30,920
-What a genius.
-Tell us what flavor you'd like,

575
00:30:31,000 --> 00:30:32,800
and we'll bring it right over!

576
00:30:32,880 --> 00:30:34,520
As for how it's made,

577
00:30:34,600 --> 00:30:36,440
-that's a secret.
-A secret?

578
00:30:36,520 --> 00:30:39,440
But that secret
is inside our spice sachets!

579
00:30:40,240 --> 00:30:41,320
The spices come from Yunnan and Guangdong

580
00:30:41,400 --> 00:30:42,880
and are made into a wet seasoning mix

581
00:30:42,960 --> 00:30:44,720
that's perfect for braised meat!

582
00:30:44,880 --> 00:30:47,360
-Just fifteen wen!
-Fifteen wen! Fifteen wen a packet!

583
00:30:47,440 --> 00:30:48,760
-I'll take one, too!
-I'll take one, too!

584
00:30:48,840 --> 00:30:50,000
-Here you are.
-Me, too!

585
00:30:50,080 --> 00:30:52,120
-Aunt Shen.
-Does it taste good?

586
00:30:52,600 --> 00:30:53,600
I've been so busy

587
00:30:53,680 --> 00:30:56,120
that I completely forgot to greet you,
so it's all my fault.

588
00:30:56,200 --> 00:30:58,520
I was wondering
where that stench was coming from.

589
00:30:59,280 --> 00:31:01,920
So Baozhu is back in her old trade,

590
00:31:02,040 --> 00:31:04,200
a butcher's daughter through and through!

591
00:31:05,440 --> 00:31:07,960
When it comes to cutting meat
and stripping bones,

592
00:31:08,040 --> 00:31:09,600
I'm second to none.

593
00:31:10,080 --> 00:31:11,280
It's good to have skills,

594
00:31:11,600 --> 00:31:13,960
but you must know your limits.

595
00:31:14,160 --> 00:31:16,000
When the wind's strong enough,

596
00:31:16,560 --> 00:31:18,600
even a pig can fly,

597
00:31:19,000 --> 00:31:20,040
but when it stops,

598
00:31:20,600 --> 00:31:21,720
won't that pig

599
00:31:22,920 --> 00:31:23,920
fall to its death?

600
00:31:25,240 --> 00:31:26,360
Then I'll collect the carcass,

601
00:31:26,440 --> 00:31:27,840
since it's my trade, after all.

602
00:31:27,920 --> 00:31:30,160
If you see one, Aunt Shen,
be sure to let me know.

603
00:31:31,000 --> 00:31:32,040
Fine,

604
00:31:32,120 --> 00:31:33,600
just you wait.
